id: pm-gh1073
title: "GH-1073: pm init accepts a whitespace id prefix that makes later creates fail"
description: "GitHub issue #1073 reports that init persists a natural-language prefix containing spaces, then every later create fails the stricter normalized-ID contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:init",github,validation
created_at: "2026-08-21T05:41:56.036Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T18:09:25.668Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T18:09:25.153Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T18:09:25.153Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Share one prefix validation primitive between SDK init and lifecycle create; fail before tracker persistence or normalize deterministically; cover CLI/SDK/MCP and packed npx/bunx behavior; document accepted prefix grammar and recovery.
parent: pm-7t04
severity: high
repro_steps: "Initialize a fresh tracker with a whitespace-containing prefix, then create an item with or without an explicit ID; observe the downstream normalization refusal."
resolution: "Resolved: init canonicalizes natural-language ID prefixes through a linear-time shared SDK contract before settings persistence and item creation."
expected_result: Init normalizes or rejects any untrusted prefix before committing tracker state without superlinear regular-expression behavior.
actual_result: The first canonicalizer used uncontrolled-data regular expressions that CodeQL identified as polynomial on long separator runs.
affected_version: 2026.8.20
component: tracker initialization
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-nmzx,discovered_from,"2026-08-21T06:19:24.627Z","harness:codex","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T05:41:56.036Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-21: searched all 2,526 PM items and repository history for whitespace prefix, init prefix validation, and GitHub #1073; existing pm-nmzx covers the distinct missing prefix flag, not invalid persisted values. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1073"
  "2026-08-21T17:06:12.693Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: focused contract suite passed (9 files, 64 tests); pnpm build, TypeScript public type tests, and full ESLint passed. Full repository gates and packed-runtime acceptance are next."
  "2026-08-21T17:45:41.874Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: the shared SDK normalizePrefix contract canonicalizes whitespace/punctuation to lowercase dash-separated prefixes, rejects the empty result via the existing pm fallback, and persists exactly one trailing dash before create. Linked CLI+SDK tests passed (9/9). Fresh packed npx, bunx, and installed-SDK consumers initialized natural-language prefixes and created IDs matching their canonical prefixes. Full suite passed 551 files / 7702 tests at exact 100% coverage; package and static gates passed."
  "2026-08-21T17:49:37.962Z","harness:codex","Governance evidence correction: classified as production_defect and bound the fix to its executable negative-control test, local packed/full/static gates, and hosted static/coverage owners; no waiver used."
  "2026-08-21T18:08:10.618Z","harness:codex","Hosted review finding: CodeQL flagged the prefix-normalization regular expressions as polynomial on uncontrolled input. Replace the regex pipeline with a single-pass ASCII normalizer and add an adversarial long-separator negative control before reclosing."
  "2026-08-21T18:09:16.156Z","harness:codex","Hosted security remediation: replaced both uncontrolled-data regular expressions with a single-pass ASCII alphanumeric normalizer. A 100,000-character separator negative control, linked 10/10 tests, focused ESLint, and build pass."
